# -*- coding: utf-8 -*-
# English layer of patterns_data.py: id -> (titleEn, explanationEn, [example translations, same order as P[i]['ex']]).
# Japanese is kept as is; patterns_data.py stays the source of truth for the Spanish text.
EN = {
'svo-masu': ('わたし は X を Vます',
 'As in English, the usual sentence order is Subject – Verb – Object (S-V-O). Japanese always puts the verb LAST: Subject – Object – Verb (S-O-V). The particle は marks the topic (who or what I am talking about) and を marks the direct object (what receives the action). A verb in its ます form is the polite present/future.',
 ['I drink water.','I read the newspaper.','I buy an umbrella.','I watch TV.','I speak Japanese.','I write a letter.']),
'svo-shimasu': ('わたし は X を します',
 'する (to do) is used with many nouns: べんきょう を します (I study), しごと を します (I work), よやく を します (I make a reservation). It also works with sports: テニス を します (I play tennis). With action nouns you can also say べんきょうします (compound verb).',
 ['I study.','I work.','I play tennis.','I go shopping.','I make a reservation.','I take a walk.']),
'go-ni-ikimasu': ('わたし は PLACE に いきます',
 'With verbs of movement (いきます to go, きます to come, かえります to return) the destination is marked with に (or へ, which is read "e"). Order: Subject – Destination – Verb. The destination goes before the verb, just like the object.',
 ["I'm going to the station.","I'm going to Kyoto.","I'm going to the restaurant.","I'm going to the gym.","I'm going to the bank."]),
'noun-desu': ('X は Y です',
 'です is like "to be" in sentences with nouns and goes at the end: Subject – Noun – です. It does not change with the person (I am / you are / he is = です). は marks the topic.',
 ['I am a student.','This is water.','That person is a teacher.','Today is Saturday.','Ms. Tanaka is Japanese.']),
'adj-desu': ('X は ADJ です',
 'With adjectives the order is also Subject – Adjective – です. い-adjectives (おいしい, いそがしい, おおきい) end in い; な-adjectives (げんき, きれい, しずか) are used the same way before です. です here only adds politeness.',
 ['Mom is well (healthy).','It is hot today.','This book is interesting.',"I'm busy tomorrow.",'Tokyo is lively.']),
'noun-janai': ('X は Y じゃないです',
 'Negative of です with nouns and な-adjectives: じゃないです (more formal: ではありません). The order does not change: Subject – Noun – じゃないです.',
 ['This is not water.',"I'm not a teacher.",'That is not a clock.','Tomorrow is not Sunday.','Mom is not well.']),
'adj-kunai': ('X は ADJ くないです',
 'ONLY for い-adjectives: drop い and add くないです (おいしい → おいしくないです). な-adjectives use じゃないです. Exception: いい → よくないです.',
 ["I'm not busy tomorrow.",'This food is not spicy.','It is not cold today.','This book is not good.','This bag is not expensive.']),
'ka-question': ('〜ですか (questions)',
 'To ask a question, add か at the end; there is no need to change the word order or use a question mark. Answers: はい (yes) / いいえ (no). Question words: なに/なん (what), だれ (who), どこ (where), いつ (when), いくら (how much).',
 ['Are you a student?','Yes, I am a student.','Is this water?',"No, it isn't water.",'What time is it?',"It's half past two."]),
'no-possession': ('N1 の N2',
 'の links two nouns: N1 の N2 = "N2 of N1" (possession, belonging, topic). The order is the reverse of the English "of" phrase: you say the possessor first. にほんご の せんせい = Japanese teacher. At the end of a sentence, の can replace the noun: わたし の (mine).',
 ['My friend.','The Japanese teacher.',"This is Mary's book.","That umbrella is Ms. Tanaka's.",'The university student.']),
'kore-sore-are': ('これ / それ / あれ / どれ',
 'Demonstrative pronouns (with no noun after them): これ = this (near me), それ = that (near you), あれ = that over there (far from both), どれ = which one? (among three or more).',
 ['What is this?',"That (near you) is an umbrella.","That (over there) is a bank.",'Which one is your watch?','This is mine.']),
'kono-sono-ano': ('この / その / あの / どの + N',
 'この, その, あの, どの are ALWAYS followed by a noun (this ..., that ..., that ... over there, which ...?). They cannot be used alone: これ (alone) vs この ほん (with a noun).',
 ['This bag is expensive.','How much are those shoes?','Who is that person over there?','Which book is interesting?','This watch is new.']),
'koko-soko-asoko': ('ここ / そこ / あそこ / どこ',
 'Places: ここ = here (near me), そこ = there (near you), あそこ = over there (far from both), どこ = where? With です they work like "to be at".',
 ['This is the school.','Where is the restroom?','The bank is over there.',"That place there is a restaurant.",'Where is the station?']),
'dare-no': ('だれの N / N の です',
 'だれの = whose? It is used like "N1 の N2". In the answer the second noun can be left out: それ は たなかさん の です (it is Ms. Tanaka\'s).',
 ['Whose bag is this?',"It is Ms. Tanaka's.",'Whose notebook is that?','It is mine.']),
'mo-too': ('X も (also, too)',
 'も = "also, too". It replaces は, が and を (it is never written together with them): わたし は → わたし も. With other particles it is added: に も, で も.',
 ['I am a student too.','Are you a student too?','This is a book too.','I drink coffee too.']),
'ikura-desu-ka': ('N は いくら ですか (prices)',
 'いくら = how much does it cost? Answer: number + えん + です. Reading prices: ひゃくえん (100), せんえん (1000), いちまんえん (10,000). See numbers.json for the irregular readings (さんびゃく, ろっぴゃく, はっぴゃく, さんぜん, はっせん).',
 ['How much is the pencil?','It is fifty yen.','How much is this watch?','It is ten thousand yen.','The dictionary is eight thousand yen.']),
'kudasai': ('X を ください',
 'ください = "please give me" when asking for something. To ask for a quantity: X を NUMBER ください (コーヒー を ふたつ ください). More polite: おねがいします.',
 ['Please give me this.','A coffee, please.','The menu, please.','Excuse me, I will take this.']),
'masu-4-tenses': ('Vます / Vました / Vません / Vませんでした',
 'The four polite verb forms: ます (affirmative present/future), ました (affirmative past), ません (negative present/future), ませんでした (negative past). You get them by dropping ます from the ます form and adding the ending; see the conjugation tables.',
 ['I eat bread.','I ate bread.',"I don't eat bread.","I didn't eat bread."]),
'question-words': ('なに / だれ / どこ / いつ + Vますか',
 'Question words take the place of the answer without changing the word order: なに を (what), どこ に/で (where to / where), だれ と (with whom), いつ (when), なんじ に (at what time).',
 ['What do you drink?','Where are you going?','Who are you going with?','When are you coming back?','What time do you get up?']),
'masu-masen': ('Vます / Vません (present and future)',
 'The ます form is used for habits and for the future (there is no separate future tense): まいにち コーヒー を のみます (I drink coffee every day), あした のみます (I will drink it tomorrow). The negative is ません.',
 ["I don't drink coffee.",'I get up at seven every day.',"I'm not going to school tomorrow.","I'm watching a movie tonight."]),
'ni-he-direction': ('に / へ (destination)',
 'Destination of a movement: に or へ (へ is read "e"). Verbs: いきます, きます, かえります. With へ the direction is emphasized; with に, the point of arrival.',
 ["I'm going home.","I'm going to school.","I'm coming to Japan.","I'm going to a friend's house."]),
'de-place-action': ('PLACE で X を Vます',
 'で marks the place where an action takes place (≠ に, which marks existence or destination). Usual order: Topic – Place で – Object を – Verb.',
 ['I read a book in the library.','I drink coffee at the cafe.','I watch TV at home.','I have dinner at the restaurant.','I study Japanese at the university.']),
'ni-time': ('TIME に Vます',
 'Exact times, days of the week, dates and years take に: しちじ に, にちようび に, ごがつ ついたち に. Relative time expressions (きょう, あした, きのう, まいにち, いま, こんばん) do NOT take に.',
 ['I get up at seven.','I go to bed at ten.','I see my friend on Sunday.','I watch a movie on Saturday.',"I'm going to school tomorrow."]),
'masen-ka': ('Vませんか (invitation)',
 'Vませんか is a soft invitation ("won\'t you...?"). Answers: ええ、Vましょう / いいですね (yes, good idea) or すみません、ちょっと… (sorry, it\'s just that...).',
 ["Won't you have coffee with me?","Yes, let's.","Won't you watch a movie?","Sorry, it's a bit...","Won't you go to the park tomorrow?"]),
'frequency': ('よく / ときどき / あまり〜ません',
 'Frequency adverbs go before the verb: よく (often), たいてい (usually), ときどき (sometimes); with a negative: あまり〜ません (not much), ぜんぜん〜ません (never / not at all).',
 ['I often watch TV.',"I hardly ever drink alcohol.","I never play tennis.",'I usually get up at seven.']),
'aru-iru-ni': ('PLACE に N が あります / います',
 'Existence: PLACE に THING が あります (things, plants, buildings) / PLACE に PERSON・ANIMAL が います. Japanese order: first the place, then what exists, and the verb last. Negative: ありません / いません; past: ありました / いました.',
 ['There is a book on the desk.','There is a cat in the room.','There are a lot of people in the bookstore.','There is a wallet in the bag.','There is a bank near the station.']),
'position-words': ('N の うえ / した / なか / まえ / うしろ',
 'Relative positions: N の うえ (on top of), した (under), なか (inside), まえ (in front of), うしろ (behind), となり (next to). As with の: first the reference point, then the position.',
 ['There is a newspaper on the table.','There is a cat under the chair.','There is a supermarket in front of the station.','There is a park behind the hotel.']),
'nanimo-daremo': ('なにも ありません / だれも いません',
 'なにも (nothing) and だれも (no one) are always combined with a negative verb: なにも ありません (there is nothing), だれも いません (there is no one).',
 ['There is no one in the room.','There is nothing in the bag.','There is nothing on the table.','There is no one on the second floor.']),
'deshita': ('でした / じゃなかったです (past of です)',
 'Past of です: でした. Negative past: じゃなかったです (or ではありませんでした).',
 ['Yesterday it rained (it was a rainy day).','Yesterday was not Sunday.','The test was difficult.','The weekend was lively.']),
'mashita-masendeshita': ('Vました / Vませんでした',
 'Polite past: ました (affirmative) / ませんでした (negative). Past time expressions (きのう, せんしゅう) take no に. あう (to meet / see a person) uses に for the person.',
 ['Yesterday I met a friend.',"This morning I didn't eat anything.",'Last week I watched a movie.',"I didn't study yesterday."]),
'to-with': ('と (with / and)',
 'と has two uses: "with (someone)": ともだち と いきます; and "and" between nouns: パン と コーヒー. It does not join verbs or sentences.',
 ['I watch a movie with a friend.','Bread and coffee, please.','There is a dog and a cat.','I go shopping with Mom.']),
'ya-etc': ('N や N (and others)',
 'や lists some items while implying there are more ("and things like that"); と lists ALL the items. It only joins nouns.',
 ['On the table there are a newspaper, flowers and other things.','In the bag there are keys, books and more.','I buy bread, fruit and other things.']),
'kara-made': ('N1 から N2 まで',
 'から = from (origin / start), まで = until (limit). They work with times, dates and places: じゅうじ から じゅういちじ まで; ここ から えき まで. With から you also give a person\'s origin: チリ から きました.',
 ['I study from ten to eleven.','I go to school from Monday to Friday.','I came from Chile.','The vacation is from the fifth to the twentieth.','From when to when is the summer vacation?']),
'adj-past': ('ADJ かったです / くなかったです',
 'い-adjectives in the past: drop い and add かったです (affirmative) / くなかったです (negative). いい → よかったです. な-adjectives use でした / じゃなかったです.',
 ['Yesterday it was hot.','The movie was not interesting.','Dinner was delicious.','The test was difficult.','The trip was good.']),
'adj-modifying': ('ADJ + N (adjective before a noun)',
 'The adjective goes BEFORE the noun, with no particles: おおきい いぬ (a big dog). な-adjectives take な: きれいな へや (a clean / pretty room), しずかな まち (a quiet town).',
 ["It's a big dog.",'I bought a new bag.','This is a nice room.','Kyoto is a quiet town.',"It's an old watch."]),
'suki-kirai': ('N が すき / きらい です',
 'すき (to like) and きらい (to dislike) are な-adjectives: what you like is marked with が (NOT with を). だいすき = I love it, だいきらい = I hate it.',
 ['I like cats.',"I don't like fish.",'I love meat.',"I don't like coffee."]),
'mashou': ('Vましょう / Vましょうか',
 'Vましょう = "let\'s V" (a proposal / accepting an invitation). Vましょうか = "shall we V?" (making a proposal). It is the natural answer to Vませんか.',
 ["Let's go back together.",'What shall we eat?',"Let's eat sushi.",'Where shall we meet?',"Let's meet at seven."]),
'de-means': ('MEANS で Vます',
 'で marks the means or instrument: でんしゃ で (by train), バス で (by bus), タクシー で (by taxi). On foot is あるいて いきます. To ask: なん で いきますか.',
 ['I go by train.','I go to school by bus.','I go to Osaka by bullet train.','I go back by taxi.','How are you going?']),
'date-desu': ('きょう は X がつ Y にち です',
 'Dates: month (がつ) + day (にち / ついたち, ふつか, みっか… はつか), from larger to smaller. Days of the week: ～ようび. Questions: なんがつ, なんにち, なんようび, いつ.',
 ['Today is May 5th.','My birthday is July 20th.','Tomorrow is Wednesday.','The meeting is on Monday.','What day is the festival?']),
'nanji-desu-ka': ('いま なんじ ですか (telling time)',
 'Telling time: number + じ (o\'clock) and はん (half past). Irregular: よじ (4), しちじ (7), くじ (9). ごぜん = a.m., ごご = p.m. Minutes: ふん / ぷん (see numbers.json).',
 ["It's half past five.","It's twelve o'clock.","It's four in the afternoon.","It's nine in the morning.","It's seven o'clock."]),
'counters': ('Counters: つ / にん / かい / さい',
 'Counters go AFTER the noun and the particle: コーヒー を ふたつ ください. Objects: ひとつ…とお; people: ひとり, ふたり, さんにん…; floors: いっかい, にかい, さんがい; age: いっさい… How many?: いくつ / なんにん / なんがい / なんさい.',
 ['Two coffees, please.','There are two of us.','I have three friends (there are three friends).','The restroom is on the second floor.','Two curries, please.']),
'doko-desu-ka': ('N は どこ ですか (where is it?)',
 'Asking for a location: N は どこ ですか. Answer with ここ / そこ / あそこ or with directions: ひだり (left), みぎ (right), まっすぐ (straight).',
 ['Where is the ticket (office)?','Where is the station?',"It's on the left.","It's over there, on the right."]),
'dono-gurai': ('どのぐらい かかりますか',
 'かかります = it takes / it costs (time or money). どのぐらい (or どのくらい) = about how much? Answer: time + かかります: じゅうごふん かかります (it takes 15 minutes).',
 ['How long does it take to get to the station?','It takes fifteen minutes.','How long does it take by train?','It takes one hour.']),
'te-kudasai': ('Vて ください',
 'Vて ください = "please do V" (polite request). て form: group I: う/つ/る→って, む/ぶ/ぬ→んで, く→いて, ぐ→いで, す→して (いく→いって is an exception). Group II: る→て. する→して, くる→きて.',
 ['Please open the window.','Please sit here.','Please speak slowly.','Please wait.','Please turn left.','Please take the Ginza line.']),
'te-form-connect': ('Vて、V (actions in sequence)',
 'The て form links actions in order. Only the last verb carries the tense (ます/ました): おきて、あびて、いきます.',
 ['I get up, take a shower and go to school.','I go to the store and buy bread.','I drink coffee and read the newspaper.']),
'te-mo-ii': ('Vても いいです',
 'Vても いいです = "it is OK to V / you may V". With か it asks for permission: Vても いいですか. Affirmative: はい、いいです; negative: いいえ、いけません.',
 ['May I eat here?','Yes, you may.','May I take photos?','May I use the phone?']),
'te-wa-ikemasen': ('Vては いけません',
 'Vては いけません = "you must not V / it is forbidden to V". It is the negation of permission. Used for rules and prohibitions.',
 ['You may not take photos here.','You may not eat in the room.','You may not enter here.','You may not smoke here.']),
'kara-because': ('S1 から、S2 (because)',
 'から after a sentence gives the reason: "S1 から、S2" = "because S1, S2" (the reason comes first and から attaches to the end of that sentence). あつい から みず を のみます.',
 ["Because it's hot, I drink water.","Because there is a test tomorrow, I study.","Because I'm busy, I'm not going."]),
'mashou-ka-offer': ('Vましょうか (offering help)',
 'Vましょうか also offers help: "shall I do it for you?". Answers: おねがいします (yes, please) / だいじょうぶです (no need).',
 ['Shall I open the window for you?','Yes, please.','Shall I carry your luggage?','Shall I turn on the light?']),
'te-imasu': ('Vて います (action in progress)',
 'Vて います = action in progress ("is doing") or resulting state (すんで います = I live in, しって います = I know).',
 ["I'm reading a book.",'I live in Tokyo.','My friend is studying at school.',"I'm waiting at the station."]),
'tai-desu': ('Vたいです (wanting to do)',
 'Vたい = "to want to V" (drop ます from the ます form and add たい). たい conjugates like an い-adjective: たいです (I want to), たくないです (I don\'t want to), たかったです (I wanted to). The object can be marked with を or が.',
 ['I want to go to Japan.','I want to drink coffee.','I want to watch a movie.','I want to see my friends.',"I don't want to eat today."]),
}
